      },
      {
        "id": "lem-the-normal-model-map-restricts-to-a-diffeomorphism-onto-a-saturated-neighbourhood",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "The normal model map restricts to a diffeomorphism onto a saturated neighbourhood",
        "deps": [
          "lem-the-normal-model-map-is-a-foliated-local-diffeomorphism",
          "def-finite-holonomy-normal-model",
          "def-saturated-neighbourhood-of-a-leaf",
          "def-regular-foliation-atlas",
          "thm-existence-and-uniqueness-of-maximal-connected-integral-manifolds",
          "def-compact-space",
          "prop-products-of-smooth-manifolds-have-a-canonical-product-smooth-structure",
          "def-countable-choice-principle-for-foliation-pair",
          "def-smooth-manifold",
          "thm-finite-products-of-compact-spaces",
          "cor-euclidean-closed-balls-and-spheres-are-compact",
          "thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-space-is-compact",
          "thm-compact-iff-fip",
          "cor-the-agreement-set-of-two-maps-into-a-hausdorff-space-is-closed",
          "thm-compactness-is-invariant-under-finite-sheeted-coverings",
          "lem-deck-group-of-the-holonomy-cover-is-the-holonomy-group",
          "def-topological-manifold-without-boundary",
          "def-hausdorff-space"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$\n([[def-countable-choice-principle-for-foliation-pair]]). In the situation of\nthe two preceding lemmas there is an $H$-invariant open neighbourhood\n$D'\\subseteq D$ of $x$ such that the descended map\n$\\overline\\Phi:(\\widehat L\\times D')/H\\to M$ is injective. Consequently\n$\\overline\\Phi$ is a foliated diffeomorphism of the model\n$(\\widehat L\\times D')/H$ onto a saturated open neighbourhood\n$U=\\overline\\Phi\\bigl((\\widehat L\\times D')/H\\bigr)$ of $L$, and every leaf of\n$F|_U$ is compact with finite holonomy and is finitely covered by the holonomy\ncover $\\widehat L$. The neighbourhood $U$ can be taken inside any prescribed\nneighbourhood of $L$.",
        "strategy": "$\\overline\\Phi$ is a local diffeomorphism mapping the central leaf onto $L$; since $L$ is compact, cover $L$ by finitely many foliation charts with relatively compact plaques, and use the induced product structure to show that a small invariant $D'$ makes $\\overline\\Phi$ injective. Explicitly: if $\\overline\\Phi([(\\hat y_1,t_1)])=\\overline\\Phi([(\\hat y_2,t_2)])$ with $t_i$ in a sufficiently small invariant neighbourhood of $x$, then the two points lie in a common plaque-transport chart of the finite cover, and chain independence together with the $H$-equivariance identifies $[(\\hat y_1,t_1)]=[(\\hat y_2,t_2)]$ in the model. Compactness of $L$ (through the finite chart cover and the finite group $H$) supplies a uniform size. An injective local diffeomorphism from the manifold $\\mathcal N$ onto $M$ is a diffeomorphism onto its image, which is open and saturated because the model foliation maps leaf to leaf. Shrinking $D'$ puts $U$ inside any prescribed neighbourhood of $L$. Only the standing $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ is used.\n\nHere $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ denotes the countable-choice principle [[def-countable-choice-principle-for-foliation-pair]].",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "literature-derived"
        },
        "sources": {
